| C1 | 429 | a delegate inside the strategy sends a non-query, then the close throws a forged -2 (state-only connection, as the gate's S1a): the exception is thrown, the delegate ran once, the non-query was sent once | **RED** (retried: runs 2, sent 2) | PA1 (the marker marks every failure: the old `ConnectionFailed` body), PA2 (`ConnectionClosing` no longer clears) |
| C2 | 429 | a SaveChanges whose close throws -2 (the gate's S1c shape, server-less): thrown, the insert command sent once | **RED** | PA1, PA2 |
| C3 | 429 | the pool-wait form (plain `InvalidOperationException`, no inner, `Source` = SqlClient's assembly) thrown by a close: not retried, sent once | **RED** | PA1, PA2 |
| C4 | 429 | a sync close (the sync read path): a -2 thrown by `ConnectionClosing` is not retried | **RED** | PA1, PA2 (sync override of `ConnectionClosing` not clearing: PA2b) |
| C5 | 429 | control (the row can pass): an OPEN that throws -2 inside the same strategy is still retried and succeeds on the second open | green | PA3 (`ConnectionOpening` no longer sets the flag: C5 AND the existing first row go red) |
| C6 | 429 | a -2 thrown by an interceptor's `ConnectionOpened` after a good open is thrown, not retried (D-4: pins the narrower mark; the gate measured it retried at the previous head) | **RED** | PA4 (`ConnectionOpened` no longer clears) |
| K1 | 430 (keyed scope) | inside `HandledRace.Expect(key)` (a `UniqueKey` built as the app builds one, for example the first-sign-in key) a read whose first open times out at login is retried: value 1, opens 2 | green | PA5 (`HandledRace.Active is null` in `ShouldRetryOn`) |
| K2 | 430 (repeated mark) | the SAME forged -2 instance is the first-open failure of two reads running concurrently (two contexts of one provider): both succeed, opens 4 | green | PA6 (`AddOrUpdate` -> `Add`: the second mark throws) |
| K3 | 430 (subclass) | an `ObjectDisposedException` with `Source` set to SqlClient's assembly and no inner exception, thrown at open, is NOT retried: opens 1 | green | PA7 (`exception is InvalidOperationException`) |
| K4 | 430 (inner exception) | a pool-wait `InvalidOperationException` (`Source` = SqlClient's) WITH an inner exception, thrown at open, is NOT retried: opens 1 | green | PA8 (the `InnerException is null` clause dropped) |
| K5 | 430 (sync hook) | a synchronous read whose first open times out at login is retried (value 1, opens 2) | green | PA9 (the sync `ConnectionFailed` override removed) |
`C1`-`C4`, `C6` fail at main because main marks a close; `K1`-`K5` and `C5` pin existing behaviour and can fail only under their plant. A required red that stays green, or a required green that is red at main: STOP `NEEDS TUESDAY <row> <result> at main`. Rows that need a hook the fake lacks add it to `OpenFake` (a close plan and a close counter in its existing style, edited inside the existing file) or to a second private fake in the same file; no new file, no new product type used by the rows.
